The seven answers jointly require a subject that is not a person, has no connection to the United States, Europe, Asia or Africa, is not tied to any particular place, and has nothing to do with aviation.

Virtually every article fails at least one of those tests:
- biographies fail the first question;
- American teams, films, programmes, court cases, buildings and historic districts fail the United States question;
- Spanish, British, Norwegian, Hungarian, Portuguese, Swedish, Polish, Lithuanian and Belgian subjects fail the Europe question;
- Japanese, Indian, Kazakh, Syrian, Filipino, Qatari and Korean subjects fail the Asia question;
- South-African, Kenyan and Cameroonian subjects fail the Africa question;
- Australian, New-Zealand, Brazilian, Honduran and Galápagos subjects fail the “specific geographic location” question;
- the Visual Glide Slope Indicator (and the 1962 air crash) fail the aviation question.

After all of those exclusions only one article remains: the biochemical definition of a response regulator (a family of proteins found in bacteria, archaea, fungi and plants). It is not a person, it has no national or continental affiliation, it is not located anywhere in particular, and it has no link to aviation.

GUESS: 114
